            <ArticleTitle>Sensitive detection of microRNAs by duplex specific nuclease-assisted target recycling and pyrene excimer switching.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10596-10599</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06290g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Herein, we develop a simple fluorescence method for the sensitive detection of microRNAs based on duplex specific nuclease-assisted target recycling and pyrene excimer switching. This method is extremely sensitive with a detection limit of 0.58 fM, and it can be applied to absolutely detect endogenous microRNAs in cancer cells, holding great potential for clinical diagnosis and biomedical research studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
